IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `scja-core`
IMPORT `scja1-part3-div3-sicc`

-- Tests for scja1-part3-div3-sicc.l4 (ss 18A to 18M). Expected values are written from the text (SCJA1969.txt lines 1317-1660), not from the code.

§ `Fixtures`

`a Judge of the High Court` MEANS Judge OF "HC", `Judge of the High Court`, Date 1 1 2015
`a Judicial Commissioner` MEANS Judge OF "JC", `Judicial Commissioner`, Date 1 1 2020
`a Senior Judge` MEANS Judge OF "SJ", `Senior Judge`, Date 1 1 2010
`an International Judge` MEANS Judge OF "IJ", `International Judge`, Date 1 1 2016
`a Justice of the Court of Appeal` MEANS Judge OF "JCA", `Justice of the Court of Appeal`, Date 1 1 2012

§§ `s 18A: the Singapore International Commercial Court`

#ASSERT (`s 18A the court is the division of the General Division known as the Singapore International Commercial Court` `Singapore International Commercial Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18A the court is the division of the General Division known as the Singapore International Commercial Court` `General Division`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18A the court is the division of the General Division known as the Singapore International Commercial Court` `Court of Appeal`) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 18B: the President of the Singapore International Commercial Court`

-- (1): a Supreme Court Judge (here a Judge of the High Court, and a Justice of the Court of Appeal), a Senior Judge, or an International Judge
#ASSERT (`s 18B(1) the Chief Justice may appoint the Judge to be the President of the Singapore International Commercial Court` `a Judge of the High Court`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18B(1) the Chief Justice may appoint the Judge to be the President of the Singapore International Commercial Court` `a Justice of the Court of Appeal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18B(1) the Chief Justice may appoint the Judge to be the President of the Singapore International Commercial Court` `a Senior Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18B(1) the Chief Justice may appoint the Judge to be the President of the Singapore International Commercial Court` `an International Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a Judicial Commissioner is outside the three named classes
#ASSERT (`s 18B(1) the Chief Justice may appoint the Judge to be the President of the Singapore International Commercial Court` `a Judicial Commissioner`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): if no appointment is made under (1), the Chief Justice is the President
#ASSERT (`s 18B(2) the Chief Justice is the President of the Singapore International Commercial Court` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18B(2) the Chief Justice is the President of the Singapore International Commercial Court` TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 18C: the Act applies with modifications`

#ASSERT (`s 18C the provision of the Act applies to proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court as to the General Division in its original civil jurisdiction` FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18C the provision of the Act applies to proceedings in the Singapore International Commercial Court as to the General Division in its original civil jurisdiction` TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 18D: jurisdiction`

-- (1): all three conditions; any one missing is the text's no ("any action that satisfies all of the following conditions")
#ASSERT (`s 18D(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear and try the action` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear and try the action` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear and try the action` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear and try the action` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (2): "without limiting (1)": met gives a yes; unmet leaves the question open
#ASSERT (`s 18D(2)(a) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear the proceedings relating to international commercial arbitration` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(2)(a) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear the proceedings relating to international commercial arbitration` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18D(2)(b) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear the application` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(2)(b) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear the application` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18D(2)(c) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear the corporate insolvency, restructuring or dissolution proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(2)(c) the Singapore International Commercial Court has jurisdiction to hear the corporate insolvency, restructuring or dissolution proceedings` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(c): the Companies Act 1967 "as in force immediately before 30 July 2020": a date before 30 July 2020 is within it, 30 July 2020 itself is not
#ASSERT (`s 18D(2)(c) the version of the Companies Act 1967 is one in force before 30 July 2020` (Date 29 7 2020)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(2)(c) the version of the Companies Act 1967 is one in force before 30 July 2020` (Date 30 7 2020)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(2)(c) the version of the Companies Act 1967 is one in force before 30 July 2020` (Date 31 7 2020)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3): "Where" the Court has and exercises jurisdiction under (1)
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3) the jurisdiction under section 18D(1) includes the further jurisdiction in this subsection` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3) the jurisdiction under section 18D(1) includes the further jurisdiction in this subsection` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(a) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the action upon the joinder of an additional party` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(a) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the action upon the joinder of an additional party` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(a) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the action upon the joinder of an additional party` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(b) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the counterclaim` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(b) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the counterclaim` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(b) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the counterclaim` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(b) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the counterclaim` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (3)(c): third party proceedings; inputs: exercising, brought against a non-party, Rules' requirements, international and commercial as a whole
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(c) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the third party proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(c) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the third party proceedings` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(c) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the third party proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(c) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the third party proceedings` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not proceedings of the kind the paragraph describes: not covered
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(c) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the third party proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(d) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the subsequent party proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(d) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the subsequent party proceedings` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(d) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the subsequent party proceedings` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(d) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the subsequent party proceedings` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(3)(d) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the subsequent party proceedings` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (4): (3)(d) applied one step on
#ASSERT (`s 18D(4) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the proceedings brought by a subsequent party` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(4) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the proceedings brought by a subsequent party` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18D(4) the jurisdiction includes hearing and trying the proceedings brought by a subsequent party` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 18F: effect of a jurisdiction agreement`

-- inputs: term, agreement to submit, express contrary provision, recourse can be validly waived
#ASSERT (`s 18F(1) the parties are considered to have agreed to the term` `s 18F(1)(a) to submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Singapore International Commercial Court` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18F(1) the parties are considered to have agreed to the term` `s 18F(1)(b) to carry out any judgment or order of the Singapore International Commercial Court without undue delay` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18F(1) the parties are considered to have agreed to the term` `s 18F(1)(c) to waive any recourse to a court or tribunal outside Singapore against any judgment or order, and against its enforcement, insofar as the recourse can be validly waived` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (c) goes only as far as the recourse can validly be waived
#ASSERT (`s 18F(1) the parties are considered to have agreed to the term` `s 18F(1)(c) to waive any recourse to a court or tribunal outside Singapore against any judgment or order, and against its enforcement, insofar as the recourse can be validly waived` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): "only if there is no express provision to the contrary"
#ASSERT (`s 18F(1) the parties are considered to have agreed to the term` `s 18F(1)(a) to submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Singapore International Commercial Court` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18F(1) the parties are considered to have agreed to the term` `s 18F(1)(b) to carry out any judgment or order of the Singapore International Commercial Court without undue delay` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no agreement to submit to the Court's jurisdiction: the section does not speak
#ASSERT (`s 18F(1) the parties are considered to have agreed to the term` `s 18F(1)(a) to submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the Singapore International Commercial Court` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `ss 18G and 18H: composition of the Court`

#ASSERT (`s 18G the proceeding is to be heard and disposed of before this number of Judges, as the section requires` 1) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18G the proceeding is to be heard and disposed of before this number of Judges, as the section requires` 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18G the proceeding is to be heard and disposed of before this number of Judges, as the section requires` 2) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18G the proceeding is to be heard and disposed of before this number of Judges, as the section requires` 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18G the proceeding is to be heard and disposed of before this number of Judges, as the section requires` 0) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 18H(1)
#ASSERT (`s 18H(1) section 18H applies to the case` 3) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18H(1) section 18H applies to the case` 1) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 18H(2)
#ASSERT (`s 18H(2) the presiding Judge was appointed by the Chief Justice, as the section requires` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18H(2) the presiding Judge was appointed by the Chief Justice, as the section requires` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18H(2) the presiding Judge was appointed by the Chief Justice, as the section requires` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 18H(3): majority of the 3 Judges
#ASSERT `s 18H(3) how the case is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 2, 1) EQUALS `s 18H(3) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, for the claim, counterclaim or application`
#ASSERT `s 18H(3) how the case is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 3, 0) EQUALS `s 18H(3) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, for the claim, counterclaim or application`
#ASSERT `s 18H(3) how the case is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 1, 2) EQUALS `s 18H(3) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, against it`
#ASSERT `s 18H(3) how the case is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 0, 3) EQUALS `s 18H(3) in accordance with the opinion of the majority, against it`
-- no majority (nobody decided, or an even division): the Act does not say
#ASSERT `s 18H(3) how the case is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 1, 1) EQUALS `s 18H(3) not covered`
#ASSERT `s 18H(3) how the case is decided` (`Split of opinion` OF 0, 0) EQUALS `s 18H(3) not covered`
-- 18H(4): inputs are Judges unable to continue, and the parties' consent to the remaining 2 continuing
#ASSERT (`s 18H(4) the case is to be reheard` 0 FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18H(4) the case is to be reheard` 1 FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18H(4) the case is to be reheard` 2 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18H(4) the case is to be reheard` 3 FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Subject to subsection (5)": one Judge unable and the parties consent: the remaining 2 may continue, so the Act does not say that the case is reheard
#ASSERT (`s 18H(4) the case is to be reheard` 1 TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 18H(5)
#ASSERT (`s 18H(5) the remaining 2 Judges may continue to hear and determine the case` 1 TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18H(5) the remaining 2 Judges may continue to hear and determine the case` 1 FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18H(5) the remaining 2 Judges may continue to hear and determine the case` 2 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18H(5) the remaining 2 Judges may continue to hear and determine the case` 0 TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- 18H(6)
#ASSERT (`s 18H(6) this subsection applies to the case` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18H(6) this subsection applies to the case` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 18H(6) how the case heard by 2 Judges is determined` (`Split of opinion` OF 2, 0) EQUALS `s 18H(6)(a) determined according to the opinion the 2 Judges share`
#ASSERT `s 18H(6) how the case heard by 2 Judges is determined` (`Split of opinion` OF 0, 2) EQUALS `s 18H(6)(a) determined according to the opinion the 2 Judges share`
#ASSERT `s 18H(6) how the case heard by 2 Judges is determined` (`Split of opinion` OF 1, 1) EQUALS `s 18H(6)(b) the claim, counterclaim or application is dismissed`
-- not a case of 2 Judges: not covered
#ASSERT `s 18H(6) how the case heard by 2 Judges is determined` (`Split of opinion` OF 2, 1) EQUALS `s 18H(6) not covered`

§§ `s 18I: powers of the Court`

-- inputs: a power the General Division may exercise in its original civil jurisdiction, paragraph 1 of the First Schedule (the seam), a power exercised through the Family Division
#ASSERT (`s 18I(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may exercise the power` TRUE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18I(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may exercise the power` TRUE (JUST TRUE) FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18I(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may exercise the power` TRUE (JUST FALSE) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the First Schedule's answer is not given: the exception is neither met nor excluded
#ASSERT (`s 18I(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may exercise the power` TRUE NOTHING FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- a power the General Division could not exercise in its original civil jurisdiction: outside the grant
#ASSERT (`s 18I(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may exercise the power` FALSE (JUST FALSE) FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- the Family Division exception holds whatever the First Schedule says
#ASSERT (`s 18I(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may exercise the power` TRUE NOTHING TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18I(2) the Singapore International Commercial Court exercises the power as the Act requires` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18I(2) the Singapore International Commercial Court exercises the power as the Act requires` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 18J: transfer of cases`

#ASSERT (`s 18J(4) the court is the General Division for the purposes of section 18J` `General Division`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18J(4) the court is the General Division for the purposes of section 18J` `Singapore International Commercial Court`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18J(4) the court is the General Division for the purposes of section 18J` `Court of Appeal`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18J(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may transfer the case to the General Division` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18J(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may transfer the case to the General Division` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18J(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may transfer the case to the General Division` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18J(2) the General Division may transfer the case to the Singapore International Commercial Court` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18J(2) the General Division may transfer the case to the Singapore International Commercial Court` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18J(2) the General Division may transfer the case to the Singapore International Commercial Court` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (3): "Where a case is transferred under (1) or (2)"
#ASSERT (`s 18J(3)(a) the court to which the case is transferred may permit a matter that has been adduced to remain in evidence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18J(3)(a) the court to which the case is transferred may permit a matter that has been adduced to remain in evidence` FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT (`s 18J(3)(b) the courts may make the consequential order` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18J(3)(b) the courts may make the consequential order` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18J(3)(b) the courts may make the consequential order` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `ss 18K and 18L: rules of evidence; foreign law`

#ASSERT (`s 18K(1)(a) the Singapore International Commercial Court is not bound to apply the rule of evidence under Singapore law` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18K(1)(a) the Singapore International Commercial Court is not bound to apply the rule of evidence under Singapore law` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18K(1)(b) the Singapore International Commercial Court may apply other rules of evidence` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18K(1)(b) the Singapore International Commercial Court may apply other rules of evidence` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2): "includes": the two named classes yes, anything else not decided
#ASSERT (`s 18K(2) the rule is a rule of evidence for the purposes of section 18K(1)` FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18K(2) the rule is a rule of evidence for the purposes of section 18K(1)` FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18K(2) the rule is a rule of evidence for the purposes of section 18K(1)` TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18K(2) the rule is a rule of evidence for the purposes of section 18K(1)` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18L(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may order the question of foreign law determined on the basis of submissions instead of proof` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18L(1) the Singapore International Commercial Court may order the question of foreign law determined on the basis of submissions instead of proof` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18L(2) the Singapore International Commercial Court may have regard to the matter in determining foreign law on submissions` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18L(2) the Singapore International Commercial Court may have regard to the matter in determining foreign law on submissions` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 18M: representation by foreign lawyers and law experts`

-- inputs: party to a case in the Court or an appeal from it, registered foreign lawyer or law expert, in accordance with the Rules of Court
#ASSERT (`s 18M the party may be represented by the foreign lawyer or law expert` TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT (`s 18M the party may be represented by the foreign lawyer or law expert` TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18M the party may be represented by the foreign lawyer or law expert` TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`s 18M the party may be represented by the foreign lawyer or law expert` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
